# Raw captures as CSV text: byte-for-byte the same samples as the .npz beside
# them, but ~1000x larger (a 1.2 M-sample capture is ~25 MB as CSV versus
# ~30 kB compressed). The scripts only write them when asked with --csv, and
# any .npz can be re-exported at any time. The .npz files themselves ARE
# committed — they are the measurement data.
*.csv
